  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Starka komuner: Svensk-schweizisk gemensam insats</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strong municipalities: Swedish-Swiss joint intervention - Strong municipalities granting Swedish-Swiss joint intervention</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;dja kommuner i Albaniens resultatuppf&#xf6;ljning och lokalt deltagande.

Det &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;let &#xe4;r att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra styrningen och serviceleveransen p&#xe5;
kommunal niv&#xe5; till f&#xf6;rm&#xe5;n f&#xf6;r albanska medborgare, i enlighet med &#xf6;verenskomna
l&#xe4;gsta och &#xf6;verkomliga standarder f&#xf6;r ett h&#xe5;llbart landsystem.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting municipalities of Albania&apos;s performance monitoring and local participation.

The overall goal is to improve governance and service delivery at the
municipal level in benefit of Albanian citizens, in accordance with agreed
minimum and affordable standards for a sustainable country system.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall goal of BtF2 is to improve governance and service delivery at the municipal level in benefit of Albanian citizens, in accordance with agreed
minimum and affordable standards for a sustainable country system. The project envisions realizing its goal by working to achieve three outcomes
namely:
(i) Municipal administrations improve service delivery (waste management &amp; preschool) towards more appropriate and affordable standards. The project will
work towards the achievement of this outcome by facilitating implementation of national service standards, offering technical assistance to municipalities that are implementing the different measures, and by supporting public participation/consultation on service delivery. The impact of project outputs is monitored and assessed by reviewing a wide range of reports, protocols, participant lists, model applications, capacity building offers, and content produced by a wide range of actors such as the municipalities, Ministries, and media.

 (ii) Municipal councils oversee adequately the performance of municipal administrations and engage in evidence-based decision-making. This will be
achieved by on the one hand offering Councillors technical support and capacity building to support them in fulfilling their mandate and secondly, by employing
project activities designed to establish effective communication channels between citizens and councillors and to support relevant system actors in policy
development and knowledge sharing with municipal councils.

 (iii) Having a new municipal performance management system and a performance-based grant in place. This activity revolves around two pillars:
firstly, its about supporting (technical/capacity building) and facilitating relevant actors (stakeholders) in designing and implementing a performance
management system and subsequently to support the monitoring and assessment of performance reports generated therein. The second pillar
revolves around the creation and implementation of a performance-based grant scheme (PBGS), whereby the project will facilitate multi-stakeholder discussions on the design of the PBGS as well as supporting the implementation and monitoring of the grant scheme by means of technical assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
